// THE WINDOWS TARGET AT x86-64-v3 (ADR 0142): the x86_64 member with its ISA
// taken at the psABI's third level, AVX2, BMI1, BMI2, FMA and MOVBE over the
// baseline's SSE2. A member of the family (ADR 0122): every fact, realization
// and header of `windows` holds of it, since the level only adds operations.
// A program built for it runs only on a machine that has the level, which is
// the portability kernels-research §6 Q2 trades for speed; `windows` stays the
// baseline.
glue windows

// THE CPU (ADR 0142), its triple's model's data, printed as every function's
// "target-cpu".
cpu "x86-64-v3"
